- How to optimize to near O(nk) for special input patterns? 
- How to reconstruct actual substrings efficiently and handle ties?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model interval scheduling with a cap on concurrent starts, a common real-world constraint in job scheduling and ad campaigns.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a limit on number of intervals
- Preprocessing next[i] via binary search
- DP with reconstruction pointers for actual selection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch for dp and reconstruction
function maxProfitTasks(s, d, p, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const idx = [...Array(n).keys()].sort((a,b)=> s[a]-s[b]);
  // reorder s,d,p by idx as needed; compute next[] with binary search
  const next = Array(n).fill(n);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) {
    let limit = s[i] + d[i] - 1;
    // binary search for first j with s[j] > limit
    let lo=i+1, hi=n; while (lo<hi){
      let mid=(lo+hi)>>1; if (s[mid] > limit) hi=mid; else lo=mid+1; }
    next[i] = lo;
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(false));
  for (let i=n-1;i>=0;i--) {
    for (let t=1;t<=k;t++) {
      if (dp[i+1][t] >= p[i] + dp[next[i]][t-1]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i+1][t];
        take[i][t] = false;
      } else {
        dp[i][t] = p[i] + dp[next[i]][t-1];
        take[i][t] = true;
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {profit: dp[0][k], take, next};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Simulates real-world budget allocation: maximize revenue from non-overlapping campaigns with a fixed cost. Tests a DP over prefixes with a per-segment penalty and reconstruction need.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and campaign count
- Inner-max optimization to O(nk)
- Path reconstruction for window endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxRevenue(daily, k, C){
  const n = daily.length; const P=[0];
  for(let x of daily) P.push(P[P.length-1]+x);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const best=Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity);
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++) best[t]=-Infinity;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t];
      best[t]=Math.max(best[t], dp[i-1][t-1]-P[i-1]);
      dp[i][t]=Math.max(dp[i][t], best[t]+P[i]-C);
    }
  }
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

